---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TAGLINE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About Yeh Bro"
	description="Yeh Bro is a fitness lifestyle brand for people who take training seriously but don’t take themselves too seriously — training, fuel, recovery, culture, and shop."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<article class="prose-wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>Yeh Bro</h1>
		<p class="about-tagline">{SITE_TAGLINE}</p>
		<p class="lede">
			A fitness lifestyle brand for people who take their training seriously but don’t take
			themselves too seriously. Training, nutrition, supplementation, gym culture, and products
			around the lifestyle. Straightforward information. Useful tools. Good gear. No unnecessary
			bullshit.
		</p>

		<h2>Who it’s for</h2>
		<p>
			Men who train and care about physique, nutrition, gymwear, energy drinks, and culture —
			everyday lifters, not only stage bodybuilders. If the gym is part of how you live, you’re in
			the right place.
		</p>

		<h2>What you get</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Train</strong> — <a href="/start-here">Yeh Bro System</a>, PPL / PPLU templates,
				weekly checklists
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Fuel</strong> — <a href="/food-bro">Food Bro</a> (scaled meals + shopping list),
				food and sports-nutrition guides
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Recover</strong> — sleep, deloads, fatigue literacy
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Culture</strong> — gym culture and PED harm-reduction education (not sourcing)
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Shop</strong> — apparel, legal sports nutrition, energy, accessories —{' '}
				<a href="/shop">coming soon</a>
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>How we talk</h2>
		<p>
			Confident, direct, knowledgeable, a bit of humour. Not a generic PT site, not clinical
			wellness theatre, not shouty grind-bro slogans. Guide-first — like an experienced gym mate,
			not an affiliate pitch.
		</p>

		<h2>Culture literacy (later, not first)</h2>
		<p>
			Bodybuilding has a pharmacology shadow. Pretending it doesn’t exist helps nobody. Leading
			beginners with it helps fewer. When you’re ready, we teach risks, bloodwork as clinical care,
			and legality at a high level — as <strong>education</strong>, not a protocol and not a
			storefront.
		</p>
		<p>
			Start with{' '}
			<a href="/blog/bodybuilding-culture-education">bodybuilding culture</a> and{' '}
			<a href="/blog/ped-harm-reduction-australia">PED harm reduction</a> after the basics. Prefer a
			clinician who knows your history.
		</p>

		<h2>Products we mention</h2>
		<p>
			When a guide links a tub, it’s legal sports nutrition — creatine, protein, pre/basics —
			judged on labels, dose clarity, and value. Quiet <code>/go/</code> links may earn a
			commission; full detail on <a href="/disclosure">Disclosure</a>. We don’t source AAS, SARMs,
			peptides, or underground gear.
		</p>

		<div class="cta-row">
			<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/start-here">Yeh Bro System</a>
			<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/food-bro">Food Bro</a>
			<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/shop">Shop</a>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about-tagline {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.35rem);
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--yb-lime);
		margin: -0.25rem 0 1.25rem;
	}
</style>
